<title>SOUTH KOREA: Kolon Construction '96 net profit falls.</title>
<headline>Kolon Construction '96 net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(In billion unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (won)			     382 vs    648</p>
<p>    Net				    3.72 vs   5.57</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, par 5,000 won)</p>
<p>     common stocks (in cash)	 none vs   1.0</p>
<p>			 (in stock)	none vs   3.0</p>
<p>     preferred     (in cash)	 1.0  vs   2.0</p>
<p>			 (in stock)	none vs   3.0</p>
<p>    Turnover			   514.06 vs 447.11</p>
<p>    Profit before tax		  5.70 vs   8.11</p>
<p>    Extraordinary (both gain)     78.09 vs 177.73</p>
<p>Note - Kolon Construction Co is an affiliate of the Kolon Group. Share capital in the company rose by 3.4 million to 13.6 million shares due to dividend payment and rights issue.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
